From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:22:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-gpu-virgl: under Xen, map blobs via subregion, not
 map_fixed

Built against virglrenderer >= 1.3.0, VIRGL_HAS_MAP_FIXED makes blob
mapping use virgl_renderer_resource_map_fixed(). That only maps the blob
into the device model's address space. Under Xen the region also has to
reach the guest p2m, and only the subregion path does this: it hands the
blob over as a dma-buf before the region is added. With map_fixed the
guest cannot use host-visible blobs, and Venus in DomA fails
vkCreateInstance with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY (seen on the RPi4 with
virglrenderer 1.3.0, 2026-10-13).

When xen_enabled(), skip the map_fixed branch and use the
virgl_renderer_resource_map() subregion path. Without Xen nothing
changes. There is no switch.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [depends on this layer's Xen blob dma-buf hand-over patches]
---
 hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
index db341dba6..e61035886 100644
--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
@@ -238,6 +238,17 @@ virtio_gpu_virgl_map_resource_blob(VirtIOGPU *g,
     }
 
 #if VIRGL_HAS_MAP_FIXED
+    /*
+     * q11-xen-no-map-fixed: under Xen the region has to reach the guest p2m, which
+     * only the subregion path below does (the dma-buf hand-over before the region
+     * is added). map_fixed only maps it into qemu, and the guest then cannot use
+     * the blob: Venus fails vkCreateInstance with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY
+     * (measured on the RPi4, virglrenderer 1.3.0, 2026-10-13).
+     */
+    if (xen_enabled()) {
+        goto map_subregion;
+    }
+
     /*
      * virgl_renderer_resource_map_fixed() allows to create multiple
      * mappings of the same resource, while virgl_renderer_resource_map()
@@ -272,6 +283,9 @@ virtio_gpu_virgl_map_resource_blob(VirtIOGPU *g,
     }
 #endif
 
+#if VIRGL_HAS_MAP_FIXED
+map_subregion:
+#endif
     ret = virgl_renderer_resource_map(res->base.resource_id, &data, &size);
     if (ret) {
         qemu_log_mask(LOG_GUEST_ERROR, "%s: failed to map virgl resource: %s\n",
